.TH ZON 1 "October 2026" "zon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zon \- query and convert Zig Object Notation with jq filters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zon
.RI [ flags ] " [FILTER] [files...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a jq filter using gojq. FILTER defaults to . (identity).
Reads files in order, or standard input when no files are given.
Use - to read standard input among files. Supply an explicit filter when
passing files. Each ZON input is one document; JSON input can contain a
sequence of values. Each filter result is emitted separately.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--in " auto|zon|json
Input format (default auto). Dot-prefixed input is ZON; objects and arrays
starting with { or [ are JSON. Bare scalars try ZON, then JSON.
.TP
.BI "--to " zon|json|yaml|toml
Output format (default zon).
.TP
.B -c, --compact
Compact ZON/JSON, YAML flow style, or inline nested TOML tables.
.TP
.B -r, --raw-output
Print string results without quotes. Other results use the selected format.
.TP
.B -n, --null-input
Run once with null without reading input.
.TP
.B -S, --sort-keys
Sort object keys. Output keys are always sorted.
.TP
.B --version
Print version.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
zon . build.zig.zon
zon --to json . build.zig.zon
zon -r '.version' build.zig.zon
zon '.dependencies | keys' build.zig.zon
zon --in json --to zon . data.json
zon -n '{answer: 6 * 7}'
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
Enum literals become strings. Empty .{} becomes an array in generic decoding.
JSON output rejects NaN and infinity and replaces invalid UTF-8 string bytes.
YAML results are separated with document markers.
TOML requires one object result, cannot represent null, and requires signed
64-bit integers. Compact TOML retains a line per top-level key.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success. Nonzero on input, filter, or output errors. Diagnostics are
written to standard error. The jq halt_error function retains its exit code.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jq (1),
.BR zig (1)
